  "Question": "Five positive consecutive integers starting with \\(a\\) have average \\(b.\\) What is the average of \\(5\\) consecutive integers that start with \\(b?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(a+3\\)",
    "B": "\\(a+4\\)",
    "C": "\\(a+5\\)",
    "D": "\\(a+6\\)",
    "E": "\\(a+7\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Five consecutive integers balance around their middle number. For the integers\n\\[\na,\\ a+1,\\ a+2,\\ a+3,\\ a+4,\n\\]\nthe outer pair sums to \\(2(a+2)\\), and the next pair also sums to \\(2(a+2)\\). Including the middle term, their total is \\(5(a+2)\\), so their average is \\(b=a+2\\).\n\nIn particular, \\(b\\) is an integer. The five consecutive integers starting with \\(b\\) likewise have average \\(b+2\\). Therefore the requested average is\n\\[\nb+2=(a+2)+2=\\boxed{a+4},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
